# sign_file_schema=1
# sign = sum_sign_total / count_total over every replica-bin block; dsign = delete-one-block jackknife error
# f_neg = (1 - sign) / 2 = fraction of measured configurations with negative sign; df_neg = dsign / 2; neither is clipped
# replica_sign_mean = mean of sum_sign_r / count_r over every replica (non-positive included); replica_sign_se = sample standard error (nan for nrep=1)
# ratio_status: ok | nonpositive_total (sum_sign_total <= 0) | nonpositive_loo (a delete-one-block sign sum <= 0); observables are NaN unless ok
# sign_unresolved=1: 0 < sign <= 2 dsign; no_negative_observed=1: ph_symmetric=0 and negative_count=0 (finite sample, not a sign-free model)
